            "id": "6af170bce29b1359f0d61c6e",
            "status": "scheduled",
            "text": "Walk to the nearest star and it takes 900 million years.\n\nHow far is the nearest star? Proxima Centauri, a small red dwarf 4.24 light-years away, is so faint you can never see it without a telescope. Even light, the fastest thing there is, takes more than four years to cross the gap.\n\nPaperclip probe or radio hello: which would you send to Proxima?\n\nWatch the film: https://youtu.be/c5AdqQsnnys\n\n#HowFarIsALightYear",
